IMPORT policy

-- The nine benchmark claims (Kant et al. 2025, Appendix A.2), each built
-- from the standing preamble ("assuming all other conditions are met and no
-- other exclusions apply, where by 'other' I mean anything not referenced
-- in the query") plus the specific facts given in that query.
--
-- Fields not referenced by a given query are set to values that satisfy
-- their corresponding condition (age well under 80; no fraud; wellness
-- visit/confirmation left as NOTHING together with `hospitalization month`
-- IS 0, which the "still pending" logic in policy.l4 treats as comfortably
-- inside both Sec. 1.3 deadlines; hospital located in the United States;
-- no excluded activity).

§ `Q1 -- hospitalized by burns suffered while doing my duty as a firefighter`

q1 MEANS Claim WITH
    `age at hospitalization`                   IS 40
    `hospitalization month`                    IS 0
    `caused by sickness or accidental injury`  IS TRUE
    `hospital is in the United States`         IS TRUE
    `event arose from skydiving`               IS FALSE
    `event arose from service in the military` IS FALSE
    `event arose from service as a fire fighter` IS TRUE
    `event arose from service in the police`   IS FALSE
    `fraud or misrepresentation occurred`      IS FALSE
    `wellness visit month`                     IS NOTHING
    `wellness visit confirmation month`        IS NOTHING

#EVAL `covered` q1

